Lazar Petrovic: the goal there is to support, high-row networks that might have very low, transaction bandwidth. So.

56
00:11:46.880 --> 00:12:04.690
Lazar Petrovic: Some networks that might have maybe a few transactions per day, or maybe a few transactions per hour, something along those lines. And, the goal is just to constrain resources. So, while there are no transactions, there is no need,

57
00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:14.290
Lazar Petrovic: To, create events, to, to create blocks, to, to use up unnecessary bandwidth, that a, …

58
00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:32.540
Lazar Petrovic: that the hydro consensus node does, when… when operating under normal circumstances. So for networks like Hedera, this, is absolutely useless, because Hedera always has transactions, and so, …

59
00:12:32.790 --> 00:12:39.740
Lazar Petrovic: It is completely meaningless. But for smaller networks, this would… this could be quite valuable.

60
00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:46.140
