154
00:24:44.530 --> 00:24:52.239
Leemon Baird: Sure. So, you can do it immediately, as soon as you have reached consensus on all the events that do have transactions inside of them.

155
00:24:52.600 --> 00:25:05.969
Leemon Baird: And so, there's no setting here. You don't need a setting for how long do I wait. It's simply, if you've already reached consensus on every event you know about that has a transaction, don't create new events. And that's really all it is.

156
00:25:05.970 --> 00:25:15.390
Leemon Baird: All this mode is, is I just don't create new events. If I don't have any transactions that have come into my inputs from the users, so I have no reason to create an event for that.

157
00:25:15.430 --> 00:25:30.879
Leemon Baird: and there's nothing in memory that I need to get consensus on, so I don't need to create events to create consensus, then I have no need to create events, so I stop creating events. And if everyone stops creating events, then, by definition, we have quiesced. That's all it is.

158
00:25:30.980 --> 00:25:44.409
Leemon Baird: It's not some super complicated sleep mode, it's simply, if there's no point in creating an event, don't create an event. And then you get this nice side effect that we don't waste tons and tons and tons of bandwidth and memory.

